  "reason": "With no prior experiments completed, there is zero evidence about which modality, encoder, profile setting, or fusion strategy is most effective. The highest-priority uncertainty is establishing a performance baseline. config_001 (rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) is the simplest, most standard configuration in the space: it uses a well-understood linear encoder (PCA-2000), avoids aggregation and fusion complexity, and isolates the RNA modality's contribution. This gives a clean reference accuracy against which all other design choices (image modality, learned encoders, multiprofile aggregation, multimodal fusion) can be evaluated in subsequent experiments. Starting with the simplest viable baseline is the most information-efficient first step under a tight 10-experiment budget, as it anchors the search and prevents misattributing performance gains to complexity rather than to a specific design choice."
